awful|very-bad|ADJECTIVE|extremely bad or unpleasant|Extremely bad, unpleasant, or upsetting.|rất tệ; kinh khủng|The awful smell made us open every window.|Mùi kinh khủng khiến chúng tôi mở tất cả cửa sổ.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; stronger than simply not good.|0
gene|inherited-information|NOUN|unit of inherited biological information|A unit of inherited information carried in DNA that helps direct biological functions and characteristics.|gen|The lesson explained how a gene can affect the production of a protein.|Bài học giải thích cách một gen có thể ảnh hưởng đến việc tạo ra một protein.|Countable; a gene may influence a characteristic, but many characteristics depend on multiple genes and other factors.|0
introduction|opening-part|NOUN|opening section explaining a subject|The opening part of a text or talk that gives background and prepares the audience for what follows.|phần mở đầu; phần giới thiệu|The introduction explains why the survey was conducted.|Phần mở đầu giải thích vì sao cuộc khảo sát được thực hiện.|Countable; introduction to a text or subject identifies what is introduced.|0
introduction|making-acquainted|NOUN|act of making people acquainted|The act of telling people who someone is so that they can become acquainted.|sự giới thiệu làm quen|After a brief introduction, the visitors began asking questions.|Sau phần giới thiệu làm quen ngắn, các vị khách bắt đầu đặt câu hỏi.|Countable for an occasion; make introductions is commonly plural when presenting several people.|1
introduction|bringing-into-use|NOUN|bringing something into use or a place|The act of making something available or putting it into use for the first time in a context.|sự đưa vào; việc áp dụng|The introduction of online booking reduced queues at the desk.|Việc áp dụng đặt chỗ trực tuyến làm giảm hàng người chờ ở quầy.|Usually introduction of something into a setting; this process sense differs from the opening of a book.|2
racist|discriminatory|ADJECTIVE|showing prejudice or unfair treatment based on race|Showing prejudice or unfair treatment towards people because of their race or perceived racial identity.|phân biệt chủng tộc|The school removed a racist slogan from the noticeboard.|Nhà trường gỡ bỏ một khẩu hiệu phân biệt chủng tộc khỏi bảng thông báo.|Can describe language, beliefs, actions, or practices; refers to discrimination, not merely mentioning race.|0
racist|person-with-prejudice|NOUN|person expressing racial prejudice|A person who holds or expresses prejudice against people because of their race.|người có tư tưởng hoặc hành vi phân biệt chủng tộc|The speaker challenged a racist who had insulted the visitors.|Diễn giả phản bác một người phân biệt chủng tộc đã xúc phạm các vị khách.|Countable; an evaluative term about beliefs or behaviour, not a person's racial identity.|1
stream|small-watercourse|NOUN|small flowing watercourse|A small natural flow of water through the land.|suối; dòng nước nhỏ|We crossed the stream on a narrow wooden bridge.|Chúng tôi băng qua con suối bằng một cây cầu gỗ hẹp.|Countable; a stream is generally smaller than a river, with no single size rule implied.|0
stream|continuous-series|NOUN|continuous movement or series|A continuing flow or sequence of people, things, or events.|dòng liên tục; chuỗi liên tiếp|A stream of visitors entered the exhibition throughout the afternoon.|Một dòng khách liên tục vào triển lãm suốt buổi chiều.|Countable in a stream of plus a plural or mass noun; need not involve water.|1
